Make doctrine/orm 2.5 quiet on PHP 7.4.

doctrine/orm is pinned to 2.5 because every later release requires
symfony/console ~3.0 while this application runs on Symfony 2.8. All hunks
below are backports of fixes that are already part of doctrine/orm 2.7 and
do not change behaviour:

 * Query/Parser.php: Lexer::lookahead, Lexer::peek(), Lexer::glimpse() and
   peekBeyondClosingParenthesis() all return null once the end of the DQL
   string is reached. Reading an array offset from them raises the PHP 7.4
   notice "Trying to access array offset on value of type null", which turns
   into an exception as soon as notices are promoted to exceptions (PHPUnit,
   Symfony debug), so any DQL ending in a literal, a LIKE or a parenthesised
   condition breaks. Guard the accesses, the same way 2.7 does.

 * UnitOfWork.php: "continue" inside a switch raises a warning since PHP 7.3.
   It always behaved like "break" there, so use "break", which is what 2.7
   ships.

